     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Dear All,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">I want to analyse the TIMSS data with mirt. As you\r\nknow the data contains many many missing values. Should I impute them or IRT\r\nwill take care of missing responses? How about if I want to do exploratory and\r\nconfirmatory factor analysis? </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Best</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\">Afshin</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\"> </span></p></div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><div><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "DDYysuJAAwAJ",
   "from": "Phil Chalmers",
   "author": "b330c2028fed415b",
   "date": "2023-05-31T14:33:10Z",
   "subject": "Re: Missing data & mirt",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">If the responses are missing at random then FIML estimation is valid. If they are not, and you are aware of the causal reason why the missing responses are present (and have access to this covariate information) then multiple imputation would be the preferred strategy.<div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
